A||N||2||Ferrari355||How do I get the speakers out of the Seats?||||5||
Z||000000||Ferrari355||01-25-2000||11:52 PM||||I have been wanting to replace the speakers in my 84 SE and I can't figure out how i'm supposed to get them out. Can yuo people help my with this. I could use alot of info. Thanks, oh what size are the speakers in the seats?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||01-26-2000||12:21 AM||||take off the seat covers..... zipper at the bottom then a bunch of hog rings. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||David Gamache||01-26-2000||12:21 AM||||To remove the seat speakers you will first have to remove the seats which are held down by four 13mm nuts per seat and unplug the speaker plug.<P>Next, remove the backrest by removing the plastic back adjustment cover,two phillips screws,the #50 torx bolt on the inside and the 15mm bolts(2)on the outsde of the seat.<P>With the backrest off turn it upside down and unzip the zipper. This will expose the inside of the seat and the hog rings (C shaped). Cut the hog rings and slide out the metal rods located on the left and right. <P>Now the cover can be pealed to the headrest where there are four more hog rings. Cut these rings and the cover can be removed. The speakers are simply stuck into the foam and can be pulled out (there is generally a thin black nylon slip cloth on the top of the headrest to make factory installation of the covers easier, you can discard this). <P>The speakers are aprox 3 inch dia and can be purchased at any wal-mart or pep boys.<P>You simply reverse the process to re install. New hog rings will have to be purchased from an upholstery shop or supplier.  ||||reg||10
